<title>UK: Heavylift '96 An-124 earnings over $100m.</title>
<headline>Heavylift '96 An-124 earnings over $100m.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavylift-VolgaDnept's earnings last year from its fleet of nine Antonov 124-100 planes climbed above $100 million for the first time, the five-year old Anglo-Russian joint venture cargo airline said in a press release.</p>
<p>UK based Heavylift, part of the Norwegian industrial group Kvaerner ASA, said the joint venture now controls over 75 percent of the worldwide market for the 120 tonne capacity 124-100s.</p>
<p>Flown hours increased to 8,000 hours last year from 6,000 in 1995 reflecting higher demand in all key businesses of aerospace, aviation,, automotive, heavy engineering, oil and gas, music and relief service. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
